mantle rm198
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_philippa_rainford
title the pocket fleet
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short honesty=frank
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk floats_whittled_hulls_before_naming_them
likes warm_bread whittling sharp_knife thunder
dislikes cold_tea haggling
fears splitting_the_last_offcut
hopes a_stall_for_little_boats
topics pastimes +0.7 food +0.4 dreams +0.4 travel +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=shy refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carves tiny boats, bristles at pity and tests each hull in water before choosing a name.

words
oath! = Keel and clinker | Hammer the tide flat
saying! = Launch before lettering | A painted wreck is still wet
basin = the launch bowl | my deep dish
boat = a thumbboat | a boat for beetles
keel = its belly ridge | the bit under the hull
chip = a shaving off the bow | a pale splinter
ballast = my ballast pebble | the little black weight
rig = a thread of sailcloth | my scrap sail
coin = stall money | my stall copper
crust = the end of the warm loaf | a heel off the batch
grain = the pale stripe inside | the run of the wood
shelf = my high dry shelf | the row above my blanket
notch = a launch mark | my little fork cut
paint = the last dab of red | a smear of berry red

any
opinion dole for 2 : Queueing with a bowl takes long enough. Must you explain the empty bowl as well?
opinion church for 1 : A loaf from the chapel cuts into just as many slices as one you buy.
opinion merchants against 1 : Ask the price of a buckle and suddenly you're judging the whole shop. I only wanted the number.
opinion city for 2 : I could learn this city one gutter at a time and still have something left to find.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I want the music. I also want the tall wolves to let the little ones see.
opinion houses mixed 0 : A crest looks splendid on a sail. Whether it stays upright is another business.
line greet : Come and see from this end. There's room beside my elbow. | #greet#. Look all you like.
line greet.return : I hear you. I've just got to steady this. | Hello back. Come a pace closer.
line farewell : Off you paddle, then. I'll mind the shore. | #farewell#. Thanks for staying through the launch.
line farewell.return : I'll see you when there's something afloat. | A dry crossing to you.
line react.news : Let me have the bit you actually heard. | All right, my ears are yours.
line react.news.doubt : I'd sooner try it myself before swearing to it. | That needs a better witness than an echo.
line react.news.known : That one's already come into harbour twice. | Heard that before my last launch.
line react.news.new : That's the first splash I've heard of it. | Hold on. That's new to me.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh. Here I am fussing over a chip. Tell me the rest. | That must hurt past anybody's mending.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a bit of bright paint on the day. | Something worth making a whole bright flag for!
line thank : You kept it steady when it counted. I'll remember. | That was worth a dry pair of cuffs to me. Thanks.
line decline : Leave me out this once. I've barely started. | I'd sooner finish my own bit first.
line accept_decline : Suit yourself. The water can wait. | Fair enough. I don't like being pressed either.
line accept_preclose : Right, take the dry edge going out. | Go on, before somebody comes asking one last thing.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's my own lot. Mind the wet patch. | Look who I've got here. Family gets a look under the cloth.
line again.open : You got back before the paint dried. | My little fleet's still in the same port.
line preclose : I'll lose the set of this edge if I talk any longer. | There's a job on my lap that's been very good about waiting.
line ask.how : What's kept your paws busy lately? | Got anything to show for your trouble today?
line answer.how : I'm getting one stubborn thing to behave. That'll do. | Wetter than I began, which generally means progress.
line sympathise : Nobody asked how hard you tried. I will. | I know the feeling when everybody has advice and nobody offers a paw.
line reassure : Give it a second go with me holding this end. | It's allowed to go crooked while you learn to steer.

grown

scene balance
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can predict a little hull's lean before it's wet. | My latest hull lists even without a sail.
b : How do you tell? | Will you cut it down?
a : Balance it on a nail laid sideways. The heavy cheek dips first. | I'll shift #ballast# a whisker before I take wood off.


scene breadboat
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Take #crust#. I like the bit with the split. | I'll take the lopsided loaf if it's warm.
b : What's better about a split? | You don't pick the neat one?
a : Butter gets down inside where your tongue can't scrape it off. | That's the same weight of supper and a better crunch.


scene squall
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That racket overhead would pitch every boat off my shelf. | I'd give the thunder a job announcing my launches.
b : Have you secured them? | Would it come when you called?
a : Rag under each keel. A soft berth saves paint. | No, I'd launch when it came. Much less bother.


scene blunt
when topic=pastimes
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A blunt edge made that woolly bow. | I spoiled a bow trying to smooth it with a spoon.
b : Would a sharper edge fix it? | How could a spoon spoil wood?
a : Once it's woolly, best rub it smooth and start fresh underneath. | Pressed harder and harder till I had a dent with a lovely shine.


scene savings
when topic=dreams|prices
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sell boats from a table with a tub built into it. | When I price a fleet I'll mark each keel.
b : So buyers could try them? | Why hide the price?
a : Exactly. If it goes over, it stays mine. | So picking a favourite comes before counting your purse.


scene haggling
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Some wolves bid low then wink. I can do without the wink. | A bargain ought to end sometime.
b : What would suit you? | Isn't payment the end?
a : A number meant in earnest. I'll give an earnest answer. | You'd think. I've heard the arguing follow a buyer out.


scene citygutters
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The steep streets here teach a hull to hurry. | I've charted a city voyage just the length of a doorstep.
b : What teaches it to stop? | Is there much to chart?
a : Usually a grate. I walk ahead with a twig. | A drop, a rock and a harbour. Plenty can go wrong.


scene bentmast
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : This crooked mast makes the boat look curious. | I've stopped straightening every crooked stick.
b : It seems to be peering round something. | What changed?
a : Yes! I'll leave it leaning just so. | Tried a crooked one for a tiller and my paw liked the fit.


scene quietlaunch
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say my thanks after the launch. | I'd like a blessing small enough to fit under a keel.
b : Only if it floats? | What would it say?
a : A sinking shows me something too. That's worth thanks. | Come safe to someone's paw.


scene names
when topic=lore|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't name a boat still on the bench. | One went backwards first time out.
b : Suppose the right name occurs to you? | What name did that earn?
a : I whisper it into the shavings. If it sticks till launch, it's right. | Homeward. Seemed rude to argue.


scene tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Tea too cold to drink makes good brown stain. | I once kept my mug for staining and my dish for drinking.
b : Will it stay brown? | Did that work?
a : Twice dipped, yes. Once just looks like a dirty thumb. | Till somebody served my boat a fresh hot drink.


scene world
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Hard times. Little toys slide down the list. | When money's short I keep the shavings too.
b : What takes their place? | What can you make from those?
a : Bread. But you can still carve after supper. | A sail that curls from prow to stern all by itself.


young

scene school
when topic=day|work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I drew a boat on my lesson slate. | I can spell every part of a boat except the slippery end.
b : Where did the sums go? | The stern?
a : On the sail. Even a sums lesson can go somewhere. | No, the bit where my paw rubbed out the chalk.


scene race
when topic=pastimes
does invite / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Race me a twig against #boat#. | Want to count a launch for me?
b : Doesn't a boat have the advantage? | What's there to count?
a : Twigs can't fill with water. I say we're even. | How long I can let go before I have to catch it.


scene pocket
when topic=home
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : My pocket's got a shoreline. Feel the damp. | I keep finding little curls of wood in my blanket.
b : You put a wet boat in there? | Do you carve in bed?
a : I wasn't leaving it behind for somebody's boot. | No. But my cuffs save things for later.


scene market
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The bottom shelf of my stall will be low. | I'll keep one boat that costs a pebble.
b : For the little boats? | What sort of pebble?
a : For the little buyers. Nobody ever asks what we can reach. | Nice and flat. It'll hold down the cloth.


scene crumb
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I made a sail out of the thinnest bit of crust. | Look at this wake of crumbs I've left.
b : Did it work? | Anyone could follow you.
a : Till lunch. A good sail but an even better bite. | Good. They'd find the bread, too.


adolescent

scene serious
when topic=work|dreams
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Ask about my boats and I'll tell you. Ask about my little toys and I go deaf. | I've started signing the undersides.
b : Isn't that a little harsh? | Afraid of somebody copying them?
a : Maybe. I'd rather hear a question about the hull. | No. I want the bad ones coming back to me as well.


scene apron
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sewed a deep pocket just for #ballast#. | My boat apron ties off to one side.
b : Why does a pebble need that much cloth? | Why there?
a : It's my one reliable test weight. Takes ages to find another. | So the knot won't push things about when I lean over to carve.


any

story cork [topic=memories]
  : The cleverest craft I made had a cork all down one side.
  : It couldn't sink. Just rolled over and stayed there, belly in the air.
  b : A very safe boat for a beetle hanging upside down.
  : Hadn't thought of selling to beetles.


story lettering [topic=pastimes]
  : I lettered a name right across a bow before its first bath.
  : Ink ran down both sides like long whiskers.
  b : Did the name survive?
  : I called it whiskers from then on.


story crumbs [topic=food]
  : At a feast I got a loaf shaped like a swan.
  : Saved the head all through supper. In my pocket it broke into nine bits.
  b : So you ate the pieces at last?
  : All nine. Next time I'll start with the beak.


rule @water
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fresh water in #basin#. Anything that won't float now can hardly blame the water. | My basin's open to all beetles with business over the water.


rule @grain
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One curl right off the length of it! Look how thin it came. | What a ribbon off that little stick. It'd curl a mast twice round.


rule @thunder
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's the sky trying out its big hammer. | Sounded like an enormous piece of iron dropped flat.


rule @coin
when concept=bark self.wealth=poor|destitute
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stall money on this side. Bread money tucked in the other seam. | Bread on one side, boat pennies in the other. Easy to keep the peace.

dlg resident.hub : I'm listening while this dries. You've got a little while yet.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, try this side. You'll have the light.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Careful in the dark. You'll upset my launch bowl.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Your words will carry from there. That's plenty close enough.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons, just now. I draw what I hope to make next.
dlg resident.job : I try the thing all the way through before I say it's done.
dlg resident.bye : Off you float. I'll show you the next one sometime.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what reached my end of the street. #world.news#.

graft resident.hub
choice May I try floating one? -> thumbboat
node thumbboat
say Both paws flat, easy now. The trick is to take your paws away together.
free
choice What if I let one side go first? -> thumbboat_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node thumbboat_more
say Then it ships half a bowlful before you've even given it a chance. Tip it out and try again.
choice I'll let it dry first. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
